			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement full languages namespace with 25+ provider registrations\n\nExpand the vscode API shim in APIFactoryService with complete language server protocol support. The languages namespace now includes:\n\n- Full diagnostic collection with Map-based URI tracking\n- All major provider registrations: hover, completion, definition, references, code actions, document highlights, symbols, workspace symbols, renaming, formatting (document/range/on-type), signature help, code lenses, folding ranges, selection range, semantic tokens, inlay hints, type hierarchy, call hierarchy, linked editing, document links, color, implementation, type definition, declaration, evaluatable expression, and inline values\n- Each register*Provider method assigns a unique handle and sends registration to Mountain via gRPC, enabling the editor to dispatch feature requests back to Cocoon\n- Provider callbacks stored in Map for lookup when Mountain sends provide_* RPCs\n- setLanguageConfiguration for language-specific settings\n\nAlso add has() method to Workspace config for key existence checks, and fix inspect() to return actual Configuration values instead of undefined stubs.\n\nThis enables VS Code extensions running in Cocoon to access full LSP functionality including diagnostics, code completion, hover tooltips, refactoring, and semantic analysis.",
			"SHA": "ea64e469d45e7948f7edd33808a0acb8d9b3a299"
		},
